{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Say</b> — [he] will speak to those who bring the offering, that the nations shall say when they return, for HaShem is king. And the meaning: for HaShem settled man upon the earth." "And the meaning of <b>also it is established</b>: for HaShem is king of justice; [unlike] the overturning of [Pharaoh] — 'the earth is unpeopled,' 'all the foundations of the earth shake.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 96, :notes {1 "הפך פור read as a name (Pharaoh) per the wordplay; the two quoted phrases render the reverse of 'תכון תבל' and 'לא תמוט', likely echoing Psalms 75:4 and 82:5."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:28.577675411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}